/*
 * External oracle: XXH3-64 reference vectors.
 *
 * PROVENANCE -- read this before trusting or editing the table below.
 *
 * Every value in rtr_vectors[] was produced by the *upstream* xxHash reference
 * implementation, not by this code. Specifically: xxhash.h from xxHash v0.8.3
 * (SHA-256 17973c0dc49d9854ca26caa191f0e12f7a424b68858d9a78de3860d959d85e4b),
 * compiled with -DXXH_INLINE_ALL and called as XXH3_64bits / XXH3_64bits_with-
 * Seed over the buffer produced by rtr_fill_test_buffer(). None of them were
 * generated by the Retrigger engine, so this file is a genuine independent
 * check and not a snapshot of our own behaviour.
 *
 * Two further oracles agreed on spot checks of this table: the official
 * `xxhsum 0.8.3` CLI (XXH3 mode, on a dumped 4096-byte buffer) and the Python
 * `xxhash` 3.6.0 module (xxh3_64_intdigest). The empty-input value
 * 0x2D06800538D394C2 is the widely published XXH3-64 hash of "".
 *
 * The input is defined by rtr_fill_test_buffer in rtr_test.h -- the xxHash
 * sanity-check LCG, r = r * 2654435761 + 2654435769 seeded with 2654435761,
 * taking byte r >> 24. A vector of length N hashes the first N bytes of that
 * one sequence. Change the generator and every number here becomes wrong.
 *
 * Lengths cover every class boundary in the algorithm: 0, the 1-3 / 4-8 / 9-16
 * short paths, 17-128, 129-240, the 240/241 crossover into the long path, and
 * multiples and near-misses of the 64-byte stripe, the 256-byte streaming
 * buffer and the 1024-byte secret block, up to 1 MB.
 */

